# Concurrency: every portal action (create / decommission) edits the single
# shared desired-state file, services.yaml. When two people act at the same time,
# both PRs append to (or trim) the same file and the second one would hit a merge
# conflict and get stuck — exactly the "my service never deployed" failure.
#
# The built-in `union` merge driver resolves overlapping changes by KEEPING LINES
# FROM BOTH SIDES instead of leaving conflict markers. For concurrent service
# additions (the common case) that means both new entries survive and both PRs
# merge cleanly. GitHub honors this driver when it performs the merge.
#
# Note: reconcile re-renders everything from services.yaml and the API re-validates
# state at merge time, so the catalog stays the single source of truth even if a
# rare add/remove overlap needs a follow-up reconcile.
services.yaml merge=union
